  "chain": "inadequate engineering rigor in modification design [cause B] -> mis-wired CT creates second ground path in NAN-X01 387 relay circuit -> (Unit 1 water intrusion at load center 1E-NGN-L02 causes ground fault) -> circulating ground current develops in mis-wired circuit -> false 387 differential relay actuation trips NAN-X01 offline -> undervoltage on Unit 2 A-train / Unit 3 B-train Class 1E buses -> valid LOP actuation: EDGs, SP pumps, Unit 3 B-train AF pump start [backups: redundant B-train/A-train buses and EDGs unaffected]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Event affects Units 2 and 3 concurrently via shared startup transformer NAN-X01; Unit 1 (in refueling outage) experienced the initiating water-intrusion ground fault on load center 1E-NGN-L02, which is modeled as a parallel contributing failure mode feeding into the circulating-current failure mode alongside the CT mis-wiring, per the narrative's causal description. Block-13 identifies docket 05000529 (Unit 2); Unit node keyed to that docket per authoritative FORM-366 fields. Backups (redundant B-train/A-train buses and EDGs) were stated as unaffected/energized throughout, supporting a conceptual BACKED_UP_BY at the plant level, though narrative frames them as unaffected/independent trains rather than explicit backups to the failed train, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was asserted to avoid overreach. Previous similar LER 2021-001-01 for Unit 1 modeled as stub with key '1-2021-001' per its stated designation."
}